  "worked_solution": "Since the two angles are supplementary, the sum of their measures is equal to ${180}^{∘}.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{40}^{∘}+(5x+{20}^{∘}) & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 5x+{60}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 5x & ={120}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={24}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
